+# Legacy rewrite source registration backend handoff
+
+Implemented the allocated source slice at base `a0b239299d75b0bd64b588fe743ebe2975fb28b9`. This is the legacy rewrite prerequisite under ADR-0020. SQL remains unparsed/unexecuted; Native adoption, full expiry and release remain open. Root owns integration and canonical status.
+
+Installed Supabase CLI 2.117.0 created `20261115154855_ai_budget_source_registration.sql` under sealed empty HOME and OS network denial. The forward migration adds a private immutable source relation and atomic `ai_budget_reserve_source_next` wrapper. It preserves the strict `ai-budget/1.0.0` budget request/receipt, OP1 helper, generic reserve/transition bodies, policy descriptors and original-period accounting. OP2 includes the real analysis/version selectors and exact printable ASCII nonce with the frozen framing and UUID transform. Any retained OP1 operation for that nonce blocks an ambiguous OP2 retry, regardless of state. The check repeats after owner/source admission.
+
+Native source admission proves the actual owned analysis, expected immutable version, active root, organization and membership. Owner admission precedes source locks; reverse/prelocked paths use nonblocking retry. Independent operation INSERT, attempt INSERT and reserved-to-dispatched guards prevent generic RPC bypass. Registration and first reservation share an inner subtransaction: denied or malformed old reservation results abort the fresh registration before returning a safe envelope. Existing dispatched settlement, unknown marking and reconciliation do not need a live source. Reserved-to-released bookkeeping keeps its existing semantics.
+
+The registered full tuple and budget binding are personal metadata, without candidate text or cascading FKs. Account and exact-root retirement capture consume this actual relation before legacy inference, including reserved/unpublished operations. Existing disposition clocks remain immutable; the earliest proved root/account cause wins. Missing historical parents or clocks do not become fresh deadlines. Registration time is never used as a deletion clock. A new complete owner-wide export retains exact source/binding proof after parent deletion. The existing disposition exporter also refuses missing registered closure.
+
+Independent readiness binds 36 actual function bodies/properties, unchanged generic budget dependencies, exact enabled guards, table access denial and a metadata-only catalogue seal. The seal is initialized once from fresh schema, constraints, indexes and trigger metadata in the future migration transaction, includes its own schema, and never learns or reseals during runtime. Private helpers/table DML are denied to clients and service_role. Reserve/source-export EXECUTE remain default-denied; metadata access is separate. Actual catalog/ACL behavior has not been executed.
+
